  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_019: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.639) establishes that multiprofile + avgpool + weighted fusion is the strongest design so far. However, every multimodal experiment to date has used resnet50 as the image encoder, and the image-only baseline (config_010, resnet50) was very weak (acc=0.208), suggesting resnet50 may not extract sufficiently informative visual features for this task. config_025 tests the same proven architecture (multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool, weighted) but swaps in imagenet_vit_l, a substantially stronger image encoder. This is the highest-value next experiment because: (1) it isolates a single, completely unexplored design dimension (image encoder capacity) while holding all other proven-optimal choices fixed, (2) it has high potential upside if ViT-L captures richer morphological features, and (3) it has high information value even if it underperforms, as it would confirm that image encoder choice is not a bottleneck and redirect effort toward other variables. Under a limited budget, this single experiment resolves a major source of uncertainty about whether the current performance ceiling is driven by the image backbone."
}

